<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udayasimha of Jalor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1204–1257</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Udayasimha was the Chahamana king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalor</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in the first half of the 13th century and the most powerful ruler of his line. He extended his kingdom over much of Marwar, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nadol">Nadol</a> and Mandor, and faced invasions by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, at first submitting and later repelling the Sultanate's armies. He was also a patron of scholars.</p></div>
